Pre-existing, unrelated-to-NEARS-3631 backend data-integrity gap (regression candidate, not
a task_bug for this ticket -- verified NOT touched by NEARS-3631's own diff).

Repro: module Search (zone 2 / Abu Dhabi) -> query "White Bread Loaf" -> SR12 collapsed row
shows "From 11 AED · 2 Stores" -> expand -> "Organic Shop" (store_id=9) + "Veggie Market"
(store_id=18).

DB check:
mysql> SELECT id,name,zone_id,status,active FROM stores WHERE id IN (9,18);
9   Organic Shop    2   1   0   <- active=0 (disabled), yet surfaces in unified search
18  Veggie Market   2   1   1

Root cause: Admin/app/Models/Store.php scopeCurrentModuleZone() (introduced by NEARS-3054,
pre-existing) filters only module_id + zone_id -- never store.active/status. The item-half
query in Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/SearchController.php::unified_search() uses this
scope via ->whereHas('store', ...->currentModuleZone(...)). Confirmed via
`git diff 40531f15f~1..821100be9 -- Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/SearchController.php`:
NEARS-3631's own diff to this file is purely additive (relevance_score/product_id/type/
results merge) and does not touch this query or scopeCurrentModuleZone -- the inactive-store
leak predates this ticket.

Effect on SR12: an inactive store can inflate a collapsed group's displayed "N stores" count
and can be counted toward the "From X AED" minimum, though in this specific repro the active
store (Veggie Market) still priced lower on a raw-price basis.
